-- 9045_s4_default_categories_account_proposals.sql -- default categories (OD-CAT-1) and accounts proposed by the AI from a
-- statement with two-step approval (OD-ACC-1), Owner decisions of 2026-11-20; plus what the first real AI connection showed
-- the draft screen lacked (account and category names, the statement header).
--   NEW bnx.default_category_tree(): the built-in two-level category list (expense and income), English and Chinese, modelled on
--       the default lists of common household finance software (Owner instruction: "从 Quicken、随手记等软件抄").
--   NEW bnx.install_default_categories(p_currency char(3)): adds every missing default category in that currency (default: the
--       household's reporting currency); an active category of the same kind, currency and English name (case-insensitive) is
--       kept and reused as a parent, so the call is safe to repeat. Installer-only (no grant; called by the migration below on
--       an installed household and by deploy/install_instance.py after the install).
--   ALTER bnx_intake.account_proposal: suggested_kind, suggested_label, opening (anchor date and ledger-sign amount taken from
--       the first statement), origin_connection_id (the AI connection that proposed it).
--   NEW bnx.cmd_propose_account_from_statement (tier 1; RC-DRAFT; MCP fin.account.propose_from_statement, scope finance.draft):
--       the AI reads institution, account type, last four digits, currency, holder names and the first statement's period
--       start and opening balance; Balnexa records an identity signal and one proposal. Refused when an active account of the
--       same institution, last four and currency exists (ACCOUNT_EXISTS) or such a proposal is open (the open one is returned).
--   MODIFY bnx.cmd_resolve_account_proposal (9010): approve takes the suggested kind and label unless the member changes them,
--       sets the opening anchor from the statement, and (unless the member says no) lets the proposing AI connection see the new
--       account-currency, so it can submit the statement as the second step. Lines marked "-- 9045".
--   MODIFY bnx.q_account_proposals (9010): returns the suggestion, the institution and the proposing client; an AI connection
--       sees only its own proposals. Lines marked "-- 9045".
--   MODIFY bnx.q_ledger_accounts (9019): accounts carry reference_display (masked, last four) for matching a statement; categories
--       carry parent_id. Lines marked "-- 9045".
--   MODIFY bnx.q_draft_get_for_confirmation (9010): the account-currency and its label, the statement header of a statement draft,
--       and the name of every line's ledger account (account label or category). Lines marked "-- 9045".
-- Expand-only. Catalog: the delta block below (generated by tools/s4/catalog_build.py).
set role bnx_definer;

